  "body": "The site tests (`python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests`) run only in the `site` job of `release.yml`, after the tag. Thus guide drift is found only when the deploy fails. This happened at v0.25.0 (#3271) and again at v0.26.0 (#3763).\n\nNo gate tier runs `site/tests`. The quick, batch and release tiers of `cargo xtask gate` do not include them, and `cut.yml` stage gate does not run them.\n\nProposal (the recommended option):\n- Add a step to the release tier of `cargo xtask gate` that runs the site tests with the pinned zola 0.23.6, so that `cut.yml` stage gate fails before the tag.\n- Optional: add the same step to the batch tier, so that `post-merge.yml` finds the drift on each push to `main`.\n\nA change to `.github/workflows/` needs the maintainer's approval (AGENTS.md \"GitHub Actions minutes are budgeted\"). A change in `xtask/` is a process change.\n\nDone means: a PR that adds an operation, a post hook or a manifest property without its site page makes a gate red before the cut.\n",
